From: Io <funer@gmx.at>
Subject: [PATCH] shared/ad: return NULL, not false, from bt_ad_has_data

autoconf 2.73 (Void) makes AC_PROG_CC prefer C23; after autoreconf the
build runs with -std=gnu23, where false is a bool and no longer a null
pointer constant:

  src/shared/ad.c:1251:24: error: incompatible types when returning type
  '_Bool' but 'struct bt_ad_data *' was expected

Still unfixed upstream (master, 2026-10). Same kind of fix as upstream
da5b5b0ec ("shared/ad: fix -std=c23 build failure") for another function.
---
--- a/src/shared/ad.c
+++ b/src/shared/ad.c
@@ -1248,7 +1248,7 @@
 					const struct bt_ad_data *data)
 {
 	if (!ad)
-		return false;
+		return NULL;
 
 	return queue_find(ad->data, data_match, data);
 }
